Changes from 6.1.13 to 7.0.0 (2026-10-24)

ezodf 7 brings documents in and out of Exponential with LibreOffice as the converter again, installed and switched
on from the administration, without the 4.x conversion daemon and without the command line. Many documents are
imported at once (files, folders, ZIP archives, web addresses, feeds, cloud folders and mailboxes), any item is
exported as a document, and the extension takes part in the kernel's transfer registry.

*Added*

- Added: The Document converter page (Setup > System > Document converter, right ezodf/converter): LibreOffice
  installed with one click (the official build into var/<site>/ezodf/libreoffice/, checked against its SHA-256 and
  the OpenPGP signature of the LibreOffice build key shipped in share/keys, no root needed) or the system's
  LibreOffice; updates and removal of a downloaded build; a conversion server switched on and off on the page,
  restarted after a crash or a hanging conversion and kept running by the cron part ezodf_keepalive; a remote
  unoserver or Gotenberg as an option; test conversions of bundled samples (share/samples); limits; cleanup.
- Added: Every conversion runs in a sandbox (bubblewrap without network, only the job directory writable) with
  time, memory, file size and process limits.
- Added: Readers for Word (DOCX), spreadsheets (XLSX, ODS, CSV, TSV), presentations (PPTX, ODP), PDF (with
  pdftotext), Markdown, HTML and plain text that work without LibreOffice; archives are checked before anything is
  read, XML is never loaded from the network, and HTML keeps only allowed elements and addresses.
- Added: Import documents (Documents > Import documents): many files, a whole folder (its tree becomes folders), ZIP
  archives and web addresses at once, each converted and published by a background job, with a live page per
  import, retry of the failed documents, a new version instead of a second item when a document is imported again
  into the same place, and safe fetching of web addresses (http and https, public addresses only, size and time
  limits).
- Added: Export documents (Documents > Export documents): any item as ODT, DOCX, PDF, RTF, DOC, XHTML, EPUB or text,
  and a folder with everything below it as a ZIP in its folder tree, written by a background job. The context menu
  offers ODT, PDF and Word (DOCX).
- Added: Background jobs on the job queue (expqueue) when it is installed, else a PHP process per job
  (bin/php/ezodfjob.php).
- Added: Document formats of 7x SQLI Import 2 (when it is installed): documents of an upload or ZIP, from web
  addresses and from a feed, a WebDAV or Nextcloud folder, a Google Drive folder, a OneDrive or SharePoint folder
  and the attachments of an IMAP mailbox, with mapping into any class, dry run, schedules, undo and the run history
  of the Imports tool. Passwords and keys are names of secrets.
- Added: AI suggestions for imported documents through expai (a summary for the intro and keywords), listed on the
  import's page and written as a new version only when someone clicks Apply.
- Added: The transfer registry entry transfer.ezodf (settings/kernelservices.ini.append.php, Exponential 6.0.15 and
  later): the kernel lists the Word and OpenDocument import and export on its "Which import or export tool do I
  need?" page, in the other tools' "Looking for...?" boxes, the "Import and export" lists, an item's Import/Export
  menu and the administration's search. Older kernels ignore it.
- Added: The manual (doc/index.md) in English and German (doc/ger-de/), also in the help center of the
  administration, and German texts of the Documents pages.
- Added: The checksum list of the extension's files (share/filelist.md5) for the upgrade check of the
  administration.
- Added: Unit tests of the readers, the HTML to ODT writer, the converter layer and the import sources.

*Updated*

- Updated: odf.ini [DocumentType] ConvertTypes[] lists every format the converter takes; a site override keeps
  working and narrows the formats.
- Updated: Settings changed on the Document converter page are kept in var/<site>/ezodf/settings.json, over odf.ini.
- Updated: Messages of failed jobs on the import and export pages name no server path.
- Updated: The documents page shows the other import and export tools, as the import page does.
- Updated: Polish buttons and menu items use the infinitive, as the Exponential administration does.
- Updated: The tests with data providers also name them in a docblock, so they run on PHPUnit 9.6 (PHP 8.0) as well
  as on PHPUnit 10 and later.
- Updated: composer.json requires PHP 8.0 or later and ext-dom, and suggests expqueue, sqliimport, expai and
  ext-curl.

*Fixed*

- Fixed: OpenDocument texts with whitespace between table cells or style properties import on PHP 8, and an item
  is named without any file extension.
- Fixed: Word and RTF documents keep their body, and items with bold or italic text can be exported.
- Fixed: Exports and imports that convert a document no longer hang under Exponential Velocity (the wait for the
  conversion server's result forgets the cached file status before each look).
- Fixed: The imports table no longer redefines the translation context variable of the page that includes it, so
  the documents and imports pages no longer log "Variable 't' is already defined".

*Upgrading*

- Install 7.0.0 over 6.x, regenerate the autoloads and clear the caches. There is no update script and no schema
  change; ezodf has no tables.
- The 4.x conversion daemon (scripts/daemon.php, odf.ini [ODFImport] ConversionDaemon) is no longer needed. Sites
  that run it keep it by leaving ConversionDaemon=enabled; otherwise the new converter is used.
- New right ezodf/converter for the Document converter page; ezodf/import and ezodf/export keep their meaning.
- The PHP zip extension (ext-zip) is required: uploaded documents are checked before anything is extracted.
